ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE ACT ON THE WELFARE OF SPORTS PERSONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Act on the Welfare of Sports Persons and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Athletes Who Are Sports Persons)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2 (1) 1 (a) of the Act on the Welfare of Sports Persons (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means persons who have competed in any of the following competitions, have been registered as athletes with sports federations under the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as "sports federations") for a total of at least five years, and have been or are currently registered for at least three consecutive years. <Amended on February 19, 2026>
1. The Olympic Games organized by the International Olympic Committee and the International Paralympic Committee;
2. The Asian Games organized by the Olympic Council of Asia and the Asian Paralympic Committee;
3. World championships organized by international sports federations for individual sports;
4. The World University Games organized by the International University Sports Federation;
5. The Deaflympics organized by the International Committee of Sports for the Deaf;
6. The National Sports Festival organized by the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee under Article 33 of the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korean Sport and Olympic Committee") or by the Korea Paralympic Committee under Article 34 of that Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Paralympic Committee");
7. Nationwide competitions organized by sports federations.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), student athletes under the School Sports Promotion Act shall be excluded from sports persons: Provided, That this shall not apply to student athletes who have been selected as national team athletes under the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as "national team athletes") for the competitions specified in paragraph (1) 1 through 5.

Article 3 (Scope of Sports Instructors Who Are Sports Persons)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2 (1) 1 (b) of the Act means persons who have coached athletes who competed in any of the following competitions and who have been registered as sports instructors with sports federations for a total of at least five years:
1. The competitions listed in the subparagraphs of Article 2 (1);
2. The National Junior Sports Festival organized by the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee;
3. The National Sports Festival for Students with Disabilities organized by the Korea Paralympic Committee.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), persons who are or were public officials under the Public Officials Pension Act and persons who are or were faculty or staff members under the Pension for Private School Teachers and Staff Act shall be excluded from sports persons.

Article 4 (Scope of Referees Who Are Sports Persons)
(1) "Persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 2 (1) 1 (c) of the Act means persons who have served at least once each year for three years at any of the following competitions and who have been registered as referees with sports federations for a total of at least five years:
1. The competitions listed in the subparagraphs of Article 2 (1);
2. The National Junior Sports Festival organized by the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee;
3. The National Sports Festival for Students with Disabilities organized by the Korea Paralympic Committee.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), persons who are or were public officials under the Public Officials Pension Act and persons who are or were faculty or staff members under the Pension for Private School Teachers and Staff Act shall be excluded from sports persons.

Article 5 (Scope of Fact-Finding Surveys)
The scope of fact-finding surveys on the working conditions, living standards, and other circumstances of sports persons under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Matters concerning general characteristics, such as sex, age, and sport;
2. Matters concerning economic circumstances, such as assets, income, and type of housing;
3. Matters concerning occupational circumstances, such as employment status, type of work, and career paths after retirement;
4. Matters concerning coverage by social insurance, such as employment insurance and industrial accident compensation insurance;
5. Other matters for which a fact-finding survey is necessary to establish and implement measures needed to enhance the welfare of sports persons.

Article 6 (Requirements for Designation as Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports of the Republic of Korea)
(1) "International sporting competitions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7 (1) of the Act means the competitions specified in Article 2 (1) 1 through 4.
(2) Persons eligible for designation as persons of distinguished service to sports of the Republic of Korea under Article 7 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "persons of distinguished service to sports") shall be persons to whom any of the following has occurred during competition, training, or coaching for a competition under paragraph (1):
1. Death;
2. Development of a disability and registration as a person with a severe disability under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
3. Aggravation of an existing disability and a change in registration from a person with a non-severe disability to a person with a severe disability under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
4. Other cases in which the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism recognizes the need to designate the person as a person of distinguished service to sports, including where a person registered as a person with a severe disability under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities develops another severe disability.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), a person shall be excluded from eligibility for designation as a person of distinguished service to sports if the cause of death or severe disability falls under any of the following:
1. The person's own intentional act or gross negligence;
2. An accident, disaster, or private act unrelated to competition, training, or coaching for such competition or training.

Article 7 (Compensation for Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall provide the following support as compensation to persons of distinguished service to sports pursuant to Article 7 (2) of the Act:
1. Payment of pensions and allowances;
2. Payment of death consolation benefits;
3. Medical support;
4. Educational support;
5. Employment support;
6. Priority supply of housing;
7. Support for earning a livelihood;
8. Other support deemed necessary by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(2) Support under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be provided beginning with the month in which the date of designation as a person of distinguished service to sports under Article 7 (1) of the Act falls: Provided, That support prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall be provided beginning with the month in which the application for such support is filed.
(3) Matters necessary for the criteria for selecting recipients of support under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), the methods of providing such support, and related matters shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 8 (Scope of Surviving Family Members or Family Members of Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports)
(1) The scope of surviving family members or family members of a person of distinguished service to sports who are eligible to receive compensation payments under Article 7 (3) 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "compensation payments") shall be as follows:
1. The spouse;
2. Children;
3. Parents;
4. Grandparents who have no adult lineal descendants;
5. Minor younger siblings who have no lineal ascendants under 60 years of age and no adult siblings.
(2) If the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism finds that a surviving family member or family member of a person of distinguished service to sports under paragraph (1) falls under any of the following, the Minister may exclude that person from eligibility to receive compensation payments following examination and resolution by the Republic of Korea Committee for Examination of Designation of Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports under Article 9 (1):
1. Failure for at least one year to fulfill the obligation to support the person of distinguished service to sports;
2. Commission of a serious criminal act against the person of distinguished service to sports or that person's spouse or lineal relative by blood;
3. Abuse or other extremely improper treatment of the person of distinguished service to sports or that person's spouse or lineal relative by blood.
(3) The spouse under paragraph (1) 1 shall include a person in a de facto marital relationship: Provided, That a spouse or a person in a de facto marital relationship shall be excluded if, after marrying or entering into a de facto marital relationship with the person of distinguished service to sports, that spouse or person is or has been in a de facto marital relationship with another person.
(4) In the case of children under paragraph (1) 2, only one person adopted by the person of distinguished service to sports because that person had no lineal descendants shall be deemed an adopted child eligible as a child.
(5) In the case of parents under paragraph (1) 3, the biological father and biological mother shall be deemed the parents: Provided, That where a stepfather has raised or supported the person of distinguished service to sports, only the one of the biological father or stepfather who primarily raised or supported that person shall be deemed the father; and where a stepmother has raised or supported the person of distinguished service to sports, only the one of the biological mother or stepmother who primarily raised or supported that person shall be deemed the mother.
(6) In the case of grandparents under paragraph (1) 4, even if they have an adult lineal descendant, they shall be deemed to have no adult lineal descendant if that descendant has a disability rendering the descendant unable to support himself or herself to the extent determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, or if that descendant falls under any of the following and is performing mandatory service:
1. An active-duty soldier enlisted pursuant to Article 16 or 20 of the Military Service Act (including a noncommissioned officer appointed without volunteering);
2. A full-time reserve serviceman called up pursuant to Article 22 of the Military Service Act;
3. A conscripted police officer or an obligatory firefighter transferred to alternative service pursuant to Article 25 of the Military Service Act;
4. A social service personnel member called up pursuant to Article 29 of the Military Service Act;
5. An alternative service personnel member called up pursuant to Article 17 of the Act on Assignment to and Performance of Alternative Service.
(7) In the case of minor younger siblings under paragraph (1) 5, even if they have a lineal ascendant under 60 years of age or an adult sibling, they shall be deemed to have no lineal ascendant under 60 years of age and no adult sibling if that lineal ascendant or sibling has a disability rendering that person unable to support himself or herself to the extent determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, or falls under any of the subparagraphs of paragraph (6) and is performing mandatory service.

Article 9 (Composition of the Republic of Korea Committee for Examination of Designation of Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall appoint the chairperson, vice chairperson, and members of the Republic of Korea Committee for Examination of Designation of Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports under Article 7(3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Committee") from among the following persons:
1. A person who, after obtaining a master's degree or higher in medicine, law, or a field related to sports at a school referred to in any subparagraph of Article 2 of the Higher Education Act, holds or has held the position of associate professor or higher, or an equivalent position, for at least five years at a school referred to in any subparagraph of that Article or at an accredited research institution;
2. A person who is or has been engaged in the medical, legal, or sports field for at least seven years.
(2) The chairperson of the Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "chairperson") shall represent the Committee and exercise overall control of its affairs.
(3) A member of the Committee who falls under any of the following subparagraphs shall be disqualified from participating in the Committee's examination and resolution of the relevant matter:
1. Where the member, the member's spouse, or the member's former spouse is a party to the relevant matter (including an officer of a party if the party is a corporation, organization, or the like; hereinafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph and subparagraph 2), or is a joint holder of rights or joint bearer of obligations with a party to the relevant matter;
2. Where the member is or was a relative of a party to the relevant matter;
3. Where the member has been directly involved in the relevant matter by providing services, advice, or research, or by any other means.
(4) A party to the relevant matter may apply to the Committee to challenge a member if circumstances make it difficult to expect a fair examination by that member, and the Committee shall decide by resolution whether to accept the challenge. In such cases, the member challenged shall not participate in that resolution.
(5) A member who falls under any ground for disqualification under the subparagraphs of paragraph (3) shall recuse himself or herself from examining the relevant matter.
(6) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may dismiss a member of the Committee who falls under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Where the member becomes unable to perform his or her duties due to a mental or physical disability;
2. Where the member has committed misconduct in connection with his or her duties;
3. Where the member is deemed unfit to serve as a member due to neglect of duties, conduct impairing dignity, or any other reason;
4. Where the member personally indicates that it is difficult for him or her to perform his or her duties.

Article 10 (Operation of the Committee)
(1) Meetings of the Committee shall be convened by the chairperson when the chairperson deems it necessary or when requested by at least one-third of the members in office.
(2) Where the chairperson intends to convene a meeting of the Committee, the chairperson shall notify each member of the date, time, and place of the meeting and the matters to be examined at least seven days before the meeting; provided that, where a meeting must be convened urgently or there is an unavoidable reason, notice may be given by the day preceding the meeting.
(3) A meeting of the Committee shall be called to order with the attendance of a majority of the members in office, including the chairperson, and resolutions shall be passed by the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(4) Where the chairperson is unable to perform his or her duties due to an unavoidable reason, the vice chairperson of the Committee shall act on behalf of the chairperson; where both the chairperson and vice chairperson are unable to perform their duties due to unavoidable reasons, a member designated in advance by the chairperson shall act on behalf of the chairperson.
(5) The Committee shall have one secretary to handle its administrative affairs, and the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall designate the secretary from among public officials under the Minister's jurisdiction.
(6) Matters necessary for the operation of the Committee, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (5), shall be determined by the chairperson following a resolution of the Committee.

Article 11 (Application for Designation as a Person of Distinguished Service to Sports)
(1) A person who seeks designation as a person of distinguished service to sports pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act shall apply to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism; provided that, where a person who seeks such designation is unable to apply for designation in person or has a reason that makes doing so difficult, his or her surviving family members or family members may apply on his or her behalf.
(2) Upon receipt of an application for designation under paragraph (1), the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall decide whether to grant designation as a person of distinguished service to sports following examination and resolution by the Committee pursuant to Article 7(3) of the Act.
(3) When examining and resolving on designation as a person of distinguished service to sports under paragraph (2), the Committee shall consider the circumstances in which the national team athlete or coach died or incurred a severe disability.

Article 12 (Reporting Changes concerning Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports and Others)
(1) Persons of distinguished service to sports and surviving family members or family members eligible to receive compensation payments under Article 8 shall, where any of the following subparagraphs applies, report the relevant fact to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism without delay, accompanied by documents that can prove that fact:
1. Where the person dies;
2. Where the person loses his or her nationality;
3. Where the person falls under Article 20 or 21 of the Act;
4. Where there is a change in the surviving family members or family members eligible to receive compensation payments under Article 8;
5. Where the person has been missing continuously for at least one year, or the grounds for the person being missing have ceased to exist;
6. Where the person's name, address, or date of birth changes;
7. Where there is any other change in personal circumstances prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(2) Upon receipt of a report under paragraph (1), the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall take necessary measures, including changing the persons eligible for compensation or excluding a person from eligibility for compensation, and notify the person who filed the report of the results.

Article 13 (Types of Welfare Benefits and Criteria for Payment)
(1) The term "welfare benefits prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as rewards, medical expenses, and scholarship programs" in Article 8(1) of the Act means the following support payments (hereinafter referred to as "welfare benefits"):
1. Performance achievement rewards;
2. Living support payments;
3. Educational support payments.
(2) Persons who may be eligible to receive welfare benefits shall be as follows, by category:
1. Performance achievement rewards under paragraph (1) 1: A national team athlete who has competed and won a prize in a competition referred to in Article 2(1)1 through 5 or in any other competition recognized by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, or a coach of such a prize-winning national team athlete;
2. Living support payments under paragraph (1) 2: A national team athlete or coach who falls under any of the following items:
(a) A recipient under the National Basic Living Security Act;
(b) A person in the next-lowest income bracket under the National Basic Living Security Act;
(c) Any other person in equivalent circumstances whom the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems it necessary to provide with living support payments;
3. Educational support payments under paragraph (1) 3: A national team athlete or coach who intends to complete a program or course under any of the following items:
(a) An educational program of a graduate school under Article 29 of the Higher Education Act or a graduate school university under Article 30 of that Act;
(b) An educational program of a foreign educational institution, or a training course of a foreign training institution, in which the person intends to study abroad under the Regulations on Studying Abroad; provided that the major shall be limited to a field related to sports.
(3) Matters necessary for the payment of welfare benefits, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), including the criteria for selecting persons eligible to receive welfare benefits, the amount payable to each eligible person, and the methods and timing of payment, shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 14 (Enrollment in Insurance or Mutual Aid)
(1) The term "sports competitions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9(1) of the Act means a competition falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. A competition referred to in any subparagraph of Article 2(1);
2. A competition organized, hosted, or sponsored by a sports organization under the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as a "sports organization");
3. A competition sponsored by the Government or a local government.
(2) A person who holds or operates a competition referred to in any subparagraph of paragraph (1) shall, pursuant to Article 9(1) of the Act, obtain insurance or mutual aid coverage relating to the holding or operation of sports competitions or the safety management of sports facilities for the following persons who participate in the relevant competition:
1. Athletes and sports instructors under the National Sports Promotion Act;
2. Referees registered with a sports federation.
(3) The term "training and sports competitions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9(3) of the Act means the competitions referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 2(1) and training for which participants are called up in order to take part in those competitions.
(4) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall, pursuant to Article 9(3) of the Act, provide financial support to enable national team athletes or coaches to obtain insurance or mutual aid coverage for injuries occurring during sports instruction and sports activities.

Article 15 (Competitions Eligible for Scholarship Programs)
The term "sports competitions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10(1) of the Act means the following competitions:
1. Nationwide competitions organized by the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee or the Korea Paralympic Committee;
2. Nationwide competitions organized by sports federations.

Article 16 (Support for Senior Sports Persons)
(1) Senior sports persons who may qualify for support under Article 11(1) of the Act shall be persons aged 60 or older.
(2) The term "cases where there are grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as chronic illness or financial hardship" in Article 11(1) of the Act means any of the following cases:
1. Cases involving persons whom the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism recognizes as needing support for medical expenses, among persons who have been receiving long-term care for at least one year due to illness, injury, or other causes;
2. Cases involving persons whom the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism recognizes as needing support for living expenses, among persons falling under either of the following items:
(a) Recipients under the National Basic Living Security Act;
(b) Persons in the next-lowest income bracket under the National Basic Living Security Act.
(3) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall prescribe and publicly notify detailed criteria for determining the need for support for medical expenses or living expenses under paragraph (2), the amounts, methods, and timing of payments for each recipient, and other matters necessary to support senior sports persons.

Article 17 (Agencies Entrusted with Career Support and Business Start-up Support for Sports Persons, Etc.)
(1) The term "corporations or organizations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 12(2) of the Act means the following corporations or organizations:
1. A specialized agency for the welfare of sports persons under Article 17(1) of the Act;
2. The Korean Sport and Olympic Committee or the Korea Paralympic Committee;
3. The Seoul Olympic Sports Promotion Foundation under Article 36 of the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Sports Promotion Foundation");
4. A nonprofit corporation established under Article 32 of the Civil Act that carries out the programs set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 12(1) of the Act.
(2) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism entrusts any part of the programs set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 12(1) of the Act pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article, the Minister shall publicly notify the entrusted entity and the details of the entrusted programs.

Article 18 (Support for the Establishment and Operation of Cooperatives, Etc.)
(1) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism provides administrative support under Article 15 of the Act to sports persons who intend to establish and operate a cooperative under the Framework Act on Cooperatives or a social enterprise under the Social Enterprise Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as "cooperatives, etc."), the Minister shall select the recipients of support through an open call for applications.
(2) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may provide sports persons selected under paragraph (1) with support for the following matters:
1. Business start-up training;
2. Guidance on administrative procedures and provision of information necessary to establish cooperatives, etc.;
3. Consulting and counseling on the management of cooperatives, etc.;
4. Other matters for which the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems administrative support necessary to establish and operate cooperatives, etc.

Article 19 (Operation of the Welfare Support System for Sports Persons)
To efficiently operate the welfare support system for sports persons under Article 16(1) of the Act, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may collect and manage the following information:
1. Information about sports persons, including sex, age, sport, and records of winning prizes in competitions;
2. Information from fact-finding surveys under Article 6 of the Act;
3. Information on the designation and compensation of persons of distinguished service to sports, and related matters, under Article 7 of the Act;
4. Information on support for national team athletes or coaches, and related matters, under Article 8 of the Act;
5. Information on enrollment in insurance or mutual aid programs under Article 9 of the Act;
6. Information on scholarship programs under Article 10 of the Act;
7. Information on support for senior sports persons under Article 11 of the Act;
8. Information on career support and business start-up support for sports persons under Article 12 of the Act;
9. Information on the lending of funds under Article 13 of the Act;
10. Information on the suspension of compensation under Article 20 of the Act;
11. Information on the revocation of designation as a person of distinguished service to sports under Article 21 of the Act;
12. Information on the discontinuance of payment of welfare benefits and other payments under Article 22 of the Act;
13. Information on the recovery, under Article 23 of the Act, of compensation payments, welfare benefits, or support payments under Article 11 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "compensation and other benefits");
14. Information on the recruitment of sports persons and their job seeking;
15. Other information prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism as necessary to improve services provided using the information set forth in subparagraphs 1 through 14.

Article 20 (Designation and Revocation of Designation of Specialized Agencies for the Welfare of Sports Persons, Etc.)
(1) Pursuant to Article 17(1) of the Act, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may designate an institution that falls under any of the subparagraphs of that paragraph and meets all of the following requirements as a specialized agency for the welfare of sports persons (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized agency"):
1. Have secured at least three persons, each with at least two years of experience performing work related to the welfare of sports persons;
2. Be equipped with facilities and equipment, such as offices and computers, necessary to carry out the programs set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 18(1) of the Act.
(2) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism designates a specialized agency under paragraph (1) or revokes the designation of a specialized agency under Article 17(2) of the Act, the Minister shall post notice thereof on the website of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 21 (Programs of Specialized Agencies, Etc.)
(1) The term "mutual aid programs for sports persons prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(1)2 of the Act means the following programs:
1. Mutual aid programs relating to injuries arising in the course of sports instruction and sports activities;
2. Mutual aid programs relating to the hosting and operation of sports competitions and similar events;
3. Mutual aid programs relating to the safety management of sports facilities;
4. Other mutual aid programs determined by the head of a specialized agency with the approval of the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(2) The term "programs prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(1)5 of the Act means programs involving publicity and the operation of educational programs to protect the rights and interests of sports persons.
(3) Where the head of a specialized agency has obtained authorization for a profit-making business pursuant to Article 18(2) of the Act, the head shall formulate an implementation plan for that business and submit it to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism within 30 days from the date on which the authorization was obtained.

Article 22 (Suspension of Compensation)
(1) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism intends to suspend any of the forms of support specified in the subparagraphs of Article 7(1) of this Decree pursuant to Article 20(1) of the Act, the Minister shall hear the opinion of the relevant person of distinguished service to sports in advance.
(2) The term "offenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20(2) of the Act means offenses prescribed in the Criminal Act: Provided, That offenses committed through negligence shall be excluded.

Article 23 (Suspension of Payment of Welfare Benefits, etc. due to Conduct Impairing Dignity)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism and the head of a local government shall suspend the payment of welfare benefits or support payments under Article 11 of the Act where a person who has committed any of the acts specified in the items of Article 22(1)3 of the Act falls under either of the following:
1. Where the person has received a disciplinary disposition of suspension of qualification or a more severe disposition from a sports organization for an act specified in any of the items of Article 22(1)3 of the Act;
2. Where the person has taken an action, such as retirement, for the purpose of evading a disciplinary disposition under subparagraph 1.
(2) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism and the head of a local government intend to suspend the payment of welfare benefits or support payments under Article 11 of the Act on a ground specified in Article 22(1)3 of the Act, they may request relevant materials from the head of a sports organization to verify materials related to the disciplinary disposition.
(3) The head of a sports organization who receives a request for relevant materials under paragraph (2) shall comply with the request unless there is a special reason not to do so.

Article 24 (Recovery of Compensation and Other Benefits)
(1) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism intends to recover compensation and other benefits pursuant to Article 23(1) of the Act, the Minister shall notify the person required to return the compensation and other benefits of the following matters in writing. In such cases, the payment deadline shall be at least 30 days from the date of notification.
1. The grounds for recovery;
2. The amount to be recovered;
3. The payment deadline;
4. The institution receiving payment (hereinafter referred to as the "receiving institution");
5. The method of payment.
(2) With respect to a person who fails to return compensation and other benefits by the payment deadline under paragraph (1)3, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall issue a demand notice within 7 days from the expiration of that payment deadline, specifying a payment period of not more than 15 days.
(3) A person who receives a notification under paragraph (1) or a demand under paragraph (2) shall pay the amount to be recovered to the receiving institution by the payment deadline: Provided, That where the person is unable to make payment by that deadline due to a natural calamity, disaster, or a comparable ground, the person shall make payment within 30 days from the date on which that ground ceases to exist.
(4) A receiving institution that receives the amount to be recovered pursuant to paragraph (3) shall issue a receipt to the payer and notify the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism of that fact without delay.
(5) Matters necessary for the recovery of compensation and other benefits, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (4), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 25 (Grounds for Writing Off Compensation and Other Benefits)
The term "unavoidable grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as where the whereabouts of the person required to make repayment are unknown or the person has no property" in Article 23(3) of the Act means the following grounds:
1. Where the whereabouts of the person required to make repayment are unknown;
2. Where the person required to make repayment has no property, such as where the person has been declared bankrupt under the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act;
3. Where the extinctive prescription period for monetary claims and debts under Article 96 of the National Finance Act or the extinctive prescription period for monetary claims and debts under Article 82 of the Local Finance Act has expired.

Article 26 (Requests for Provision of Materials, etc.)
The term "materials or information prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as proof of family relationships, health insurance, and criminal history" in the main clause of Article 24(1) of the Act means the following materials or information:
1. Materials concerning the achievements, etc. of sports persons issued by sports organizations;
2. Materials concerning whether a person is enrolled, the type of enrollment, the amounts assessed, and the history of receipt of benefits under national health insurance, the national pension, employment insurance, industrial accident compensation insurance, public officials' pensions, public officials' accident compensation benefits, and pensions for private school teachers and staff members;
3. Computerized resident registration information;
4. Computerized family relationship registration information;
5. Information concerning criminal acts;
6. Materials concerning the degree of disability;
7. Materials verifying recipients of benefits and persons in the next-lowest income bracket under the National Basic Living Security Act.

Article 27 (Entrustment of Duties)
The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall entrust the following duties to the Korea Sports Promotion Foundation pursuant to Article 25(2) of the Act:
1. Payment of welfare benefits to national team athletes or coaches under Article 8 of the Act;
2. Receipt of applications for support for senior sports persons and payment of support payments under Article 11 of the Act;
3. Receipt of applications for compensation for persons of distinguished service to sports and disbursement of compensation payments under Article 7;
4. Receipt of applications for designation as a person of distinguished service to sports under Article 11(1);
5. Receipt of reports of changes concerning persons of distinguished service to sports, etc. under Article 12(1) and notification of the results of measures taken under paragraph (2) of that Article.

Article 28 (Processing of Personally Identifiable Information, etc.)
The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 26, subparagraph 5 of the Act means the following matters:
1. Designation of, and compensation for, persons of distinguished service to sports under Article 7 of the Act;
2. Support for national team athletes or coaches under Article 8 of the Act;
3. Support for obtaining insurance or mutual aid coverage under Article 9 of the Act;
4. Scholarship support under Article 10 of the Act;
5. Support for senior sports persons under Article 11 of the Act;
6. Career support and support for starting businesses for sports persons under Article 12 of the Act;
7. Lending of funds to finance preparations for starting businesses related to sports activities and to cover the costs of obtaining employment in the sports sector under Article 13 of the Act;
8. Protection of sports persons against occupational accidents under Article 14 of the Act;
9. Support for cooperatives, etc. under Article 15 of the Act.

ADDENDA <No. 32863, August 9, 2022>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on August 11, 2022.

Article 2 (Applicability to Exclusion of Surviving Family Members or Family Members of Persons of Distinguished Service to Sports)
Article 8(2) shall apply beginning with cases where surviving family members or family members of a person of distinguished service to sports commit an act falling under any of the subparagraphs of that paragraph after this Decree enters into force. In such cases, the period during which the duty of support toward a person of distinguished service to sports under subparagraph 1 of that paragraph has not been fulfilled shall be counted from the day on which that duty of support was not fulfilled after the entry into force of this Decree.

Article 3 (Amendment of Other Statutes and Regulations)
The Enforcement Decree of the National Sports Promotion Act shall be partially amended as follows:

Article 15, Articles 15-4 through 15-19, and Article 18-5 shall each be deleted.

Article 23(1)11 shall be amended as follows:

11. Expenses necessary for the measures under Article 12(1).

In subparagraph 10 of Article 23-3, "Article 22(1)6 and 11 of the Act" shall be replaced with "Article 22(1)11 of the Act".

Subparagraphs 4, 5, 7, and 8 of Article 44(2), subparagraphs 4 through 7 of Article 44-3(2), and subparagraphs 2 and 3 of Article 44-3(3) shall each be deleted.

Article 4 (Transitional Measures Following Amendment of Other Statutes and Regulations)
Research pensions for improving athletic performance and research expenses for sports instructors that, at the time this Decree enters into force, have been paid or are being paid under Article 15(2) of the former Enforcement Decree of the National Sports Promotion Act shall be deemed performance achievement rewards under Article 13(1)1.

ADDENDA <No. 36115, February 19, 2026>

This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
